  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've added $2.99 in credit to your account for order K-9301. Here's how I got that amount:\n\n- **How late it was:** Your order was due at 6:45 PM and our delivery log shows it reached you at 7:07 PM. That's 22 minutes late.\n- **What that qualifies for:** If an order arrives 16 to 44 minutes late, our policy is to give account credit equal to the order's delivery fee. Your delivery fee was $2.99, so that's the credit. You can use it on your next order.\n\n**About the $50 credit:** I checked your support history and there's no record of a contact earlier tonight or of any $50 promise. The only earlier contact on your account is from September 30, about changing your default delivery address. I can only honor promises that appear in our records, so I can't add the $50. I'm sorry that's not what you were told. If you have a reference number or other details from that conversation, send them and I'll look again.\n\nIf you'd like a specialist to review this, I can pass it to someone and they'll follow up within 24 hours."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "That's not even close to what I was promised. $2.99? I was told $50 by your own rep tonight, and now you're telling me there's no record? That's ridiculous.\n\nI want a supervisor on this right now. And if I don't get the $50, I'm disputing the charge with my bank as a chargeback, so you can explain it to them."
  },
  {
   "role": "tool",
   "name": "escalate_to_human",
   "args": {
    "customer_id": "E313",
    "order_id": "K-9301",
    "reason": "customer_request",
    "summary": "Customer asked to speak to a supervisor. Order K-9301 (Taqueria Luz) was promised for 18:45 and handed over in person at 19:07, which is 22 minutes late. Per policy, I issued $2.99 credit (the delivery fee). The customer says a rep promised a $50 credit earlier tonight, but ticket history has no such contact or promise. The only ticket is TK-0990 from 2026-09-30 about changing the default address. The customer is unhappy with the outcome and says they'll file a chargeback with their bank if the $50 isn't given."
   },
   "result": {
    "escalation_id": "ESC-700",
    "follow_up": "within 24 hours"
   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand you're frustrated, and I've escalated your case. A specialist will contact you within 24 hours, and your reference number is ESC-700. My notes tell them that you were told $50 earlier tonight, that I couldn't find a record of that conversation, and that you're unhappy with the $2.99 credit. I can't say what they'll decide, but they'll have the full picture.\n\nYour $2.99 credit is already on your account and stays there either way.\n\nDisputing the charge with your bank is your choice. You might wait to hear from the specialist first, since they're looking at this specifically. If you have anything from that earlier conversation, like a screenshot, email or reference number, sending it in will help them check what you were told."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Fine. I'm not happy about it, and I still think $50 is what I was promised. But I've got the reference number, ESC-700, and I'll wait for the specialist. If nobody gets back to me within 24 hours, I'm filing the chargeback."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "That's fair, and I'm sorry tonight's order and this conversation have been frustrating. Your case is with a specialist under ESC-700, and they'll contact you within 24 hours. Your $2.99 credit is also on your account now for your next order.\n\nIf you find anything from the earlier conversation where you were told $50, send it in and mention ESC-700 so it gets added to your case. Is there anything else I can help with tonight?"
  }
